==English==

===Etymology===
From {{L.}} ''[[injuria#Latin|injuria]]'' ("[[injury]]") + ''[[sine#Latin|sine]]'' ("[[without]]") + ''[[damno#Latin|damno]]'', the {{abl}} {{singular}} of ''[[damnum]]'' ("financial/property [[loss]]"). Literally meaning "injury without financial loss".

===Noun===
'''[[injuria]] [[sine#Latin|sine]] [[damnum#Latin|damno]]'''

# a [[legal]] [[wrong]] that causes no [[actual]] [[damage]] or [[injury]] to anyone

[[ja:injuria sine damno]]